Question 5: Use a = np.arange(1, 36).reshape(5, 7). Print the 3rd row, the 4th column, the last row and the last column.

AIM: Array slicing as specified

Code:
import numpy as np
a=np.arange(1,36).reshape(5,7)
print("3rd row:\t",a[2])
print("4th column:\t",a[:,3])
print("Last row:\t",a[-1])
print("Last column:\t",a[:,-1])

Output:
3rd row:         [15 16 17 18 19 20 21]
4th column:      [ 4 11 18 25 32]
Last row:        [29 30 31 32 33 34 35]
Last column:     [ 7 14 21 28 35]

Explanation:
Key Concept: Array Slicing- First index: rows, Second Index(after ,): columns, Indexing starts from 0 from the left and -1 from the right
